Most calls likely pass the main-field sentinel index `0xFFFF`. For that index, `subFieldIndex >= GetNumSubFields()` is always true, because the subfield count is at most 0xFFFF. So the new first check can return `GetScale()` directly and skip the subfield-count lookup. All other indices follow the original logic unchanged, so results are the same for every input.

```cpp
FIT_FLOAT64 FieldBase::GetScale(const FIT_UINT16 subFieldIndex) const
{
    if (subFieldIndex == 0xFFFF)
        return GetScale();

    if (subFieldIndex >= GetNumSubFields())
        return GetScale();

    auto subfield = GetSubField(subFieldIndex);
    return NULL != subfield ? subfield->scale : 1.0;
}
```